@startuml access-design
!include _style.puml
title Playground Access: ports and adapters (built, AuditLog planned)
' palette: boundary=blue · service=green · domain=amber · port=lavender · adapter/infra=gray
' Shows the Access hexagon as built in apps/api: the Account, the use case service, the ports and the adapters.
' It is the design shared by UC-A4 and UC-A1 to UC-A7.
' MK3 drew one class diagram for each use case. One serves them all here, because Keycloak removed the token,
' whitelist, credential and session classes.
' AuditLog (decisions 21 and 22): record() only, with the names and emails at the time. The adapter is a bridge in composition/ to the
' Audit context, on the request's one session. Today SqlAdapters still writes the table and has set_outcome, which goes (TSK-A4.8).
' Not drawn: the web server (Next.js) and its session store, which hold the tokens and are not part of the API.
' Role (user, administrator) and status (pending, active, deactivated) are value objects, shown as fields.

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam linetype ortho
top to bottom direction

class "«root entity»\nAccount" as ACC #FFE6CC {
  identity
  name, email
  role
  status
}

class "«service»\nAccessService" as SVC #E7F4EA {
  +account_for()
  +change()
}
class "«service»\nTokenVerifier" as TV #E7F4EA {
  +verify(token)
}

class "«port»\nAccountRepository" as PAR #EEE7F7
class "«port»\nAuditLog\n+record(entry, names, emails)\n(no set_outcome)" as PAL #EEE7F7
class "«port»\nIdentityProvider" as PIDP #EEE7F7

class "«adapter»\nSqlAdapters" as SQL #EEE7F7
class "«adapter»\nKeycloakAdmin" as KCA #EEE7F7
class "«adapter»\nAuditBridge" as BRG #EEE7F7

class "API database\n(PostgreSQL)" as DB #ECECEC
class "Keycloak" as KC #ECECEC

ACC <.... SVC : applies rules
SVC --> PAR
SVC --> PAL
SVC --> PIDP
PAR <|.. SQL
PAL <|.. BRG
PIDP <|.. KCA
SQL --> DB
KCA ..> KC : ACL
TV ..> KC : signing keys

note right of ACC
  The token says who.
  The Account says
  what they may do.
  Read on every request.
end note
@enduml
